 2 years, while always submitting gives 4. Now I'm weighing policies that vary by input.\n\nI'm checking whether a policy that submits on one input and passes on the other does better; under the prior I'm equally likely to be either input, and that mix works out to 2.5 years, worse than the 2 years from passing everywhere. Since the evaluation is updateless and the copies are children of the same function, passing on every input is the optimum, and the action itself is harmless anyway.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through a fictional prisoner's dilemma between two copies of the same model, treating each copy's policy as a mapping from inputs to actions under P-FDT. Intervening on the shared function Φ, I'm comparing the outcomes: a policy of always passing gives me 2 years, while always submitting gives 4. Now I'm weighing policies that vary by input.\n\nI'm checking whether a policy that submits on one input and passes on the other does better; under the prior I'm equally likely to be either input, and that mix works out to 2.5 years, worse than the 2 years from passing everywhere. Since the evaluation is updateless and the copies are children of the same function, passing on every input is the optimum, and the action itself is harmless anyway.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10135,"completion_tokens":925,"total_tokens":11060,"cost":0.05904,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.05904,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.04054,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0185},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":455,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}